item.description:
A few days ago, this paper was published in Nature [1] claiming a huge improvement in LLM inference using analog computing:
&ldquo;Our architecture reduces attention latency and energy consumption by up to two and four orders of magnitude&rdquo;
This could mean we may soon run LLMs on devices no bigger than smartphones while consuming less power than a light bulb. After taking a deep dive, I believe this might turn out to be one of the most influential results of 2025.
